# Release binding and finite source contracts

KeePass2.61.1 SourceZIP is bound by the captured publisher integrity page and SHA256`711bd9ec7076661678469e51bae876debac07a08c32f1b1c6b3b8fe5e761c13a` (5333853 bytes). The full ZIP census has1381 entries;12 selected source/license files were extracted with path/count/per-file bounds. This is a selected source study, not an exhaustive review. SourceForge mirror transport, publisher digest verification and absent OpenPGP verification are separately recorded in acquisition receipts. Failed page-selector and download attempts are preserved.

The independently preserved original executable has SHA256`04d29636c393f0c1fc99ff739295494be3adefded93271e44591e8e300225a5a`. It is loaded only by the test adapter after authentication. Tests use owned temporary paths and synthetic keys/databases. The adapter imposes a30second child deadline and1MiB per-stream capture bound. The focused recorder adds a60second child deadline and4MiB per-stream capture bound. Bounds apply to child execution/capture, not hard deadlines for fingerprint file I/O; Windows direct-child cleanup does not claim complete descendant isolation.

`contract-map.json` binds own paraphrases to exact selected release file hashes, byte spans and context hashes. `PwEntryForm.SaveEntry` establishes backup-before-change/no-op rollback/maintenance ordering. The candidate has a smaller editable field set and no unsaved dialog/event implementation. `OnBtnHistoryRestore` establishes the restore-then-touch path. Actual release library methods validate the represented data contract; source-assisted timestamp assignments make tests deterministic and are not original GUI execution.

`PwEntry.CreateBackup` clones metadata and clears history in the copy. `RestoreFromBackup` preserves the selected reference across backup/pruning and assigns properties without replacing maintained history or location metadata. `AssignProperties` defines the copied known fields. `MaintainBackups`, `RemoveOldestBackup`, `GetSize`, and `TimeUtil.Compare(...,true)` define count/size cleanup and the unknown-time ordering. `TimeUtil.SafeMaxValueUtc` explains the candidate's bounded rejection for required pruning on9999-12-31. The source defect and candidate safe rejection were identified by source inspection; no intentionally hanging original loop was executed.

The manual supplement's199 record/207 citation inventory and original159 source fingerprints/232 capability IDs are immutable separate evidence. This candidate neither replaces those records nor turns their source-only discovery receipt into implemented-feature evidence. The old compatibility18 receipt is preserved by exact SHA256 and still refers to its original eight app/source files. Production and staged source histories are not rebound.
